Input: {"question": "What position does William Henry Doveton Haggard currently or formerly hold?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "William Henry Doveton Haggard"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 31, "end": 188, "text": "Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard (1846-1926) was a British diplomat and clergyman who served as a diocesan bishop in the late 19th and early 20th centuries."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 189, "end": 213, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 215, "end": 301, "text": "Haggard was born on October 12, 1846, in London, England, to a family of modest means."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 302, "end": 413, "text": "He was educated at Eton College and later attended Christ Church, Oxford, where he earned a degree in theology."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 414, "end": 431, "text": "Diplomatic Career"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 433, "end": 538, "text": "Haggard began his diplomatic career in 1870, serving as a junior attaché at the British Embassy in Paris."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 539, "end": 714, "text": "Over the next several decades, he held various postings in Europe and Asia, including stints as Consul-General in Shanghai and Minister Plenipotentiary to the Kingdom of Siam."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 715, "end": 731, "text": "Episcopal Career"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 733, "end": 836, "text": "In 1895, Haggard was ordained as a priest in the Church of England and began his ecclesiastical career."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 837, "end": 955, "text": "He served as a chaplain to the British Embassy in Berlin before being consecrated as the Bishop of Kensington in 1902."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 956, "end": 1100, "text": "As diocesan bishop, Haggard was responsible for the pastoral care of the Diocese of Kensington, which comprised several parishes in west London."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1101, "end": 1248, "text": "During his tenure, he oversaw the construction of several new churches and implemented various reforms to improve the spiritual lives of his flock."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1249, "end": 1271, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1273, "end": 1340, "text": "Several studies have examined Haggard's life and career, including:"}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1342, "end": 1412, "text": "* \"The Diplomatic Career of Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard\" by J.M."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1413, "end": 1453, "text": "Thompson (Oxford University Press, 1932)"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1454, "end": 1525, "text": "* \"The Episcopal Ministry of Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard\" by C.H."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1526, "end": 1547, "text": "Phillips (SPCK, 1940)"}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1548, "end": 1612, "text": "* \"Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard: A Life of Service\" by P.G."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1613, "end": 1637, "text": "Rogers (Macmillan, 1965)"}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1639, "end": 1830, "text": "These studies provide a comprehensive overview of Haggard's life and career, including his diplomatic postings, his ordination and consecration as a bishop, and his tenure as diocesan bishop."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 85, "text": "\"The Diplomatic Trailblazer: The Life and Times of Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 87, "end": 239, "text": "In the late 19th century, as the British Empire was at its zenith, a remarkable individual emerged to leave an indelible mark on the world of diplomacy."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 240, "end": 524, "text": "Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard, a man of unwavering dedication and unshakeable integrity, would go on to hold the esteemed position of Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina, a testament to his exceptional skills and tireless efforts in the realm of international relations."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 525, "end": 629, "text": "Born in 1846, Haggard's early life was marked by a strong sense of adventure and a thirst for knowledge."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 630, "end": 790, "text": "His family's military background and connections to the British aristocracy instilled in him a deep understanding of the importance of diplomacy and statecraft."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 791, "end": 984, "text": "As he grew older, Haggard's fascination with languages and cultures led him to develop a remarkable proficiency in Spanish, a skill that would serve him well in his future diplomatic endeavors."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 985, "end": 1118, "text": "Haggard's entry into the world of diplomacy was marked by his appointment as a clerk in the UK Foreign & Commonwealth Office in 1867."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1119, "end": 1238, "text": "It was here that he honed his skills, working tirelessly behind the scenes to facilitate communication between nations."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1239, "end": 1386, "text": "His exceptional abilities and dedication did not go unnoticed, and he soon rose through the ranks, earning the respect and admiration of his peers."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1387, "end": 1513, "text": "In 1885, Haggard's diplomatic prowess was recognized with his appointment as Secretary of Legation in Buenos Aires, Argentina."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1514, "end": 1678, "text": "This marked the beginning of a long and fruitful association with the country, during which he would play a pivotal role in strengthening Anglo-Argentine relations."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1679, "end": 1851, "text": "His deep understanding of Argentine culture and politics, coupled with his fluency in Spanish, enabled him to navigate the complex web of international relations with ease."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1852, "end": 1934, "text": "As the years passed, Haggard's reputation as a skilled diplomat continued to grow."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1935, "end": 2077, "text": "In 1896, he was appointed Minister Plenipotentiary to Argentina, a position that cemented his status as a leading figure in British diplomacy."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2078, "end": 2281, "text": "His tireless efforts to promote British interests in Argentina, while maintaining a delicate balance between the two nations, earned him the respect and admiration of the Argentine government and people."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2282, "end": 2421, "text": "The crowning achievement of Haggard's illustrious career came in 1902, when he was appointed Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c1", "entity": "William Henry Doveton Haggard", "scope": "Former diplomatic positions", "claim": "Haggard held various postings in Europe and Asia, including stints as Consul-General in Shanghai and Minister Plenipotentiary to the Kingdom of Siam.", "answer": "Consul-General in Shanghai and Minister Plenipotentiary to the Kingdom of Siam", "quote": "Over the next several decades, he held various postings in Europe and Asia, including stints as Consul-General in Shanghai and Minister Plenipotentiary to the Kingdom of Siam.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c2", "entity": "William Henry Doveton Haggard", "scope": "Former ecclesiastical position", "claim": "He served as a chaplain to the British Embassy in Berlin before being consecrated as the Bishop of Kensington in 1902.", "answer": "Bishop of Kensington", "quote": "He served as a chaplain to the British Embassy in Berlin before being consecrated as the Bishop of Kensington in 1902.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "William Henry Doveton Haggard", "scope": "Former position", "claim": "Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard held the esteemed position of Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina.", "answer": "Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina", "quote": "Sir William Henry Doveton Haggard, a man of unwavering dedication and unshakeable integrity, would go on to hold the esteemed position of Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina, a testament to his exceptional skills and tireless efforts in the realm of international relations. Born in 1846, Haggard's early life was marked by a strong sense of adventure and a thirst for knowledge. His family's military background and connections to the British aristocracy instilled in him a deep understanding of the importance of diplomacy and statecraft. As he grew older, Haggard's fascination with languages and cultures led him to develop a remarkable proficiency in Spanish, a skill that would serve him well in his future diplomatic endeavors. Haggard's entry into the world of diplomacy was marked by his appointment as a clerk in the UK Foreign & Commonwealth Office in 1867. It was here that he honed his skills, working tirelessly behind the scenes to facilitate communication between nations. His exceptional abilities and dedication did not go unnoticed, and he soon rose through the ranks, earning the respect and admiration of his peers. In 1885, Haggard's diplomatic prowess was recognized with his appointment as Secretary of Legation in Buenos Aires, Argentina. This marked the beginning of a long and fruitful association with the country, during which he would play a pivotal role in strengthening Anglo-Argentine relations. His deep understanding of Argentine culture and politics, coupled with his fluency in Spanish, enabled him to navigate the complex web of international relations with ease. As the years passed, Haggard's reputation as a skilled diplomat continued to grow. In 1896, he was appointed Minister Plenipotentiary to Argentina, a position that cemented his status as a leading figure in British diplomacy. His tireless efforts to promote British interests in Argentina, while maintaining a delicate balance between the two nations, earned him the respect and admiration of the Argentine government and people. The crowning achievement of Haggard's illustrious career came in 1902, when he was appointed Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c1", "entity": "William Henry Doveton Haggard", "scope": "Former position", "claim": "In 1885, Haggard was appointed Secretary of Legation in Buenos Aires, Argentina.", "answer": "Secretary of Legation in Buenos Aires, Argentina", "quote": "In 1885, Haggard's diplomatic prowess was recognized with his appointment as Secretary of Legation in Buenos Aires, Argentina.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c2", "entity": "William Henry Doveton Haggard", "scope": "Former position", "claim": "In 1896, he was appointed Minister Plenipotentiary to Argentina.", "answer": "Minister Plenipotentiary to Argentina", "quote": "In 1896, he was appointed Minister Plenipotentiary to Argentina, a position that cemented his status as a leading figure in British diplomacy.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Bishop of Kensington", "Consul-General in Shanghai", "Minister Plenipotentiary to the Kingdom of Siam", "Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina", "Secretary of Legation in Buenos Aires, Argentina", "Minister Plenipotentiary to Argentina", "Chaplain to the British Embassy in Berlin", "Junior Attaché at the British Embassy in Paris", "Clerk in the UK Foreign & Commonwealth Office", "Diocesan Bishop"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Bishop of Kensington", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Consul-General in Shanghai", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "Minister Plenipotentiary to the Kingdom of Siam", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R3", "answer": "Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Argentina", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R4", "answer": "Secretary of Legation in Buenos Aires, Argentina", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R5", "answer": "Minister Plenipotentiary to Argentina", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R6", "answer": "Chaplain to the British Embassy in Berlin", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R7", "answer": "Junior Attaché at the British Embassy in Paris", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R8", "answer": "Clerk in the UK Foreign & Commonwealth Office", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R9", "answer": "Diocesan Bishop", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}

